    "title": "Two headlines show the incoherence of the West's Russia policy",
    "text": "The last few days have brought two very different Russia-related headlines from the free world that raise a serious question about the coherence, logic and indeed wisdom of Western policy toward Moscow.\nIn late August, the government of Canada announced that it is lifting travel and financial sanctions off Anatoly Chubais, a longtime confidant of Kremlin dictator Vladimir Putin. Having helped strengthen Putin’s hold on power in the early years, Chubais continued to work for him for decades, either as head of state-controlled corporations or as his personal adviser, before quietly slipping out of Russia after the start of its full-scale invasion of Ukraine in 2022. The Canadian Foreign Ministry cited unspecified “reasonable grounds” for Chubais’s delisting. It is difficult to fathom what these could be: Since leaving Russia, Chubais has not uttered a single word against Putin’s dictatorship or against his war in Ukraine.",
